<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>org.kde.kemu</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <name>KEMU</name>
  <summary>KDE QEMU Virtual Machine Manager</summary>
  <developer id="kde.org">
    <name>Marco Nelles</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      KEMU is a KDE desktop frontend for QEMU, developed using Qt6 and KDE Frameworks 6. It provides a simple, fast, and intuitive graphical interface to manage your local virtual machines without the overhead of libvirt.
    </p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Create, edit, and delete QEMU virtual machines through a graphical interface</li>
      <li>Automated Deploy feature with Cloud-Init support</li>
      <li>Snapshot support (QCOW2)</li>
      <li>Hot-swap ISO images</li>
      <li>USB device passthrough support</li>
      <li>User-mode networking via passt or QEMU's built-in SLIRP backend</li>
      <li>Rootless virtual networks within Linux user namespaces (native builds only)</li>
      <li>Shared folders via 9p/VirtFS (Linux/BSD) and virtio-fs (Windows)</li>
      <li>Portable VM directories with config.json + disk images</li>
      <li>Export and import VMs as compressed archives (.kemu.tar.zst)</li>
      <li>OVA export and import for interoperability</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
